  ('asymptotic', 'MATH', 'Approaching a value or curve arbitrarily closely as a limit', 'Asymptotic analysis characterizes algorithm efficiency as input size grows without bound', 140, 'master'),
  ('convergent', 'MATH', 'Approaching a definite limit', 'A convergent series has partial sums that approach a finite value', 140, 'master'),
  ('divergent', 'MATH', 'Failing to approach a finite limit', 'The harmonic series is divergent despite its terms approaching zero', 140, 'master'),
  ('monotonic', 'MATH', 'Consistently increasing or consistently decreasing', 'A bounded monotonic sequence necessarily converges', 140, 'master'),
  ('Cauchy sequence', 'MATH', 'A sequence whose terms become arbitrarily close to each other', 'Completeness means every Cauchy sequence converges within the space', 140, 'master'),
  ('Lebesgue measure', 'MATH', 'The standard way of assigning length/area/volume to subsets of Euclidean space', 'The Lebesgue measure of the Cantor set is zero despite its uncountable cardinality', 140, 'master'),
  ('Banach space', 'MATH', 'A complete normed vector space', 'The space of continuous functions on a closed interval forms a Banach space under the supremum norm', 140, 'master'),
  ('Hilbert space', 'MATH', 'A complete inner product space generalizing Euclidean space', 'Quantum states reside in a complex separable Hilbert space', 140, 'master'),
  ('sigma-algebra', 'MATH', 'A collection of sets closed under countable unions and complements', 'A sigma-algebra provides the domain over which probability measures are defined', 140, 'master'),
  ('measurable', 'MATH', 'Belonging to the sigma-algebra on which a measure is defined', 'Only measurable sets can be assigned a well-defined probability', 140, 'master'),
  ('Lagrangian', 'PHYS', 'A function encoding the dynamics of a system as kinetic minus potential energy', 'The principle of least action requires the physical path to extremize the Lagrangian integral', 140, 'master'),
  ('Hamiltonian', 'PHYS', 'The total energy operator generating time evolution in mechanics', 'Hamilton\'s equations give the time evolution of position and momentum in phase space', 140, 'master'),
  ('geodesic', 'PHYS', 'The shortest or extremal path between points on a curved surface', 'In general relativity, freely falling particles follow geodesics of spacetime', 140, 'master'),
  ('entanglement', 'PHYS', 'Quantum correlations between particles that persist regardless of distance', 'Entanglement enables correlations that violate Bell inequalities and defy classical explanation', 140, 'master'),
  ('superposition', 'PHYS', 'The quantum principle that a system exists in multiple states simultaneously', 'Superposition collapses upon measurement, yielding a definite outcome probabilistically', 140, 'master'),
  ('decoherence', 'PHYS', 'The loss of quantum coherence through interaction with environment', 'Environmental decoherence explains why macroscopic objects appear classical', 140, 'master'),
  ('renormalization', 'PHYS', 'A mathematical procedure removing infinities from quantum field theory calculations', 'Renormalization group methods reveal how physics changes with energy scale', 140, 'master'),
  ('perturbation', 'PHYS', 'A small disturbance to a system used to approximate solutions', 'Perturbation theory expands solutions in powers of a small coupling constant', 140, 'master'),
  ('Lagrangian density', 'PHYS', 'The Lagrangian per unit volume for a field theory', 'The Standard Model Lagrangian density encodes all known fundamental interactions', 140, 'master'),
  ('Noether's theorem', 'PHYS', 'Every continuous symmetry implies a conserved quantity', 'Noether\'s theorem connects time translation symmetry to energy conservation', 140, 'master'),
  ('gauge invariance', 'PHYS', 'Symmetry under local phase transformations of the field', 'Gauge invariance necessitates the existence of force-carrying particles', 140, 'master'),
  ('thermodynamic equilibrium', 'PHYS', 'A state of maximum entropy with no net macroscopic flows', 'Thermodynamic equilibrium is the attractor toward which isolated systems evolve', 140, 'master'),
  ('entropy', 'PHYS', 'A measure of disorder or the number of accessible microstates', 'The second law guarantees that entropy of an isolated system never decreases', 140, 'master'),
  ('ergodicity', 'PHYS', 'The property that time averages equal phase-space averages', 'Ergodicity justifies the use of statistical ensembles to predict equilibrium properties', 140, 'master'),
  ('black body', 'PHYS', 'An idealized object absorbing all incident radiation', 'Planck\'s resolution of the black body spectrum inaugurated quantum theory', 140, 'master'),
  ('wave function', 'PHYS', 'A complex-valued function encoding the quantum state of a system', 'The wave function\'s squared magnitude gives the probability density of measurement outcomes', 140, 'master'),
